1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,162
WWW.MY-SUBS.CO

﻿1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
- Synced and corrected by <font color="#009BCB"><b>chamallow</b></font> -
- www.MY-SUBS.com -

2
00:00:08,916 --> 00:00:10,499
A mountain's like a person.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,999
Sing to it properly, it will
reflect your song back to you,

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,249
showing you where to
mine, where to tunnel...

5
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:18,375
And where to leave
the mountain untouched.

6
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:21,958
Father...

7
00:00:21,959 --> 00:00:23,832
It's more than we ever imagined.

8
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:26,165
- King Durin, there is a...
- Enough!

9
00:00:26,166 --> 00:00:27,416
Seize the Elf.

10
00:00:28,375 --> 00:00:30,915
Elrond is as much a brother to me

11
00:00:30,916 --> 00:00:34,249
as if he'd been fired
in my own mother's womb.

12
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:36,040
How dare you!

13
00:00:36,041 --> 00:00:38,165
Invoke your mother's memory

14
00:00:38,166 --> 00:00:41,332
to defend your decision
to betray your own kind?

15
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:43,624
It's you that's betrayed our kind!

16
00:00:43,625 --> 00:00:46,041
You profane the crown you wear!

17
00:00:49,875 --> 00:00:51,249
Leave it.

18
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:52,750
It's not yours anymore.

19
00:00:55,125 --> 00:00:57,457
From shadow you came.

20
00:00:57,458 --> 00:01:00,083
To shadow I bid you return!

21
00:01:04,751 --> 00:01:07,624
You had that dream again
last night, didn't you?

22
00:01:07,625 --> 00:01:09,999
In the dream, there's
a kind of... branch.

23
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,374
Under the stars.

24
00:01:14,125 --> 00:01:15,500
It appears we're being followed.

25
00:01:17,626 --> 00:01:19,582
I was sifting through Sadoc's old book.

26
00:01:19,583 --> 00:01:21,540
I think it's some kinda directions.

27
00:01:21,541 --> 00:01:23,582
Welcome to the lands of Rhûn.

28
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:25,499
Why you looking at it like that?

29
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:27,040
Like you've been here before.

30
00:01:27,041 --> 00:01:28,416
Only in dreams.

31
00:01:34,458 --> 00:01:35,624
Tell me your name.

32
00:01:35,625 --> 00:01:38,207
I have had many names.

33
00:01:38,208 --> 00:01:39,540
Where is Halbrand?

34
00:01:39,541 --> 00:01:42,499
He is gone. And I doubt he will return.

35
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:45,582
And should he ever, none of
us are to treat with him again.

36
00:01:45,583 --> 00:01:49,832
Elrond just informed me your
companion was not who he claimed.

37
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:51,082
He is not what I thought.

38
00:01:51,083 --> 00:01:52,665
He is Sauron.

39
00:01:52,666 --> 00:01:55,916
It is to be given directly
to Lord Celebrimbor.

40
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:00,290
He must be informed
that Halbrand is Sauron.

41
00:02:00,291 --> 00:02:03,333
Forgive me, my lord, but a
messenger has just arrived.

42
00:02:03,833 --> 00:02:05,416
Do we grant him entry?

43
00:03:20,291 --> 00:03:24,582
- Mole-tail stew, mole-tail stew...
- Oh.

44
00:03:24,583 --> 00:03:26,040
Wait.

45
00:03:26,041 --> 00:03:27,750
- Too dear.
- What?

46
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:30,332
We're not paupers.

47
00:03:30,333 --> 00:03:33,290
You're the one said we'd be wise
to tighten our purse strings.

48
00:03:33,291 --> 00:03:36,375
Or were you not including
yourself when you said that?

49
00:03:37,166 --> 00:03:38,166
Hmm?

50
00:03:42,416 --> 00:03:44,041
You married a prince.

51
00:03:45,583 --> 00:03:47,583
But now you're bound to an outcast.

52
00:03:51,625 --> 00:03:54,625
I'm bound to the Dwarf I love.

53
00:03:56,791 --> 00:04:01,791
And I wouldn't trade his heart
for a mine full of fire opals.

54
00:04:08,708 --> 00:04:10,457
Be nice to have the opals, though.

55
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:12,374
Aye. It would.

56
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,082
Have you tried to talk to your father...

57
00:04:16,083 --> 00:04:19,499
Disa, you know he will
never agree to see me.

58
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:20,875
That's not what I asked.

59
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,665
Why should I be the one
to ask for an audience?

60
00:04:23,666 --> 00:04:25,540
He disowned me!

61
00:04:25,541 --> 00:04:28,124
He's as stubborn as a stone leg.

62
00:04:28,125 --> 00:04:30,458
You're gonna have better
luck tryna bend a brick.

63
00:04:31,291 --> 00:04:32,457
You may as well f...

64
00:04:32,458 --> 00:04:33,541
Disa?

65
00:04:34,833 --> 00:04:35,833
Brace yourself.

66
00:04:38,583 --> 00:04:40,790
I said brace yourselves!

67
00:04:40,791 --> 00:04:41,999
Disa!

68
00:05:25,541 --> 00:05:26,750
Durin.

69
00:05:28,708 --> 00:05:29,708
No.

70
00:05:31,541 --> 00:05:32,666
No, no, no, no.

71
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:19,124
These lands shall bear you

72
00:07:19,125 --> 00:07:22,750
sweet blossoms once more.

73
00:07:29,041 --> 00:07:30,500
My dear brother.

74
00:07:44,291 --> 00:07:45,541
Lord Celebrimbor.

75
00:07:47,416 --> 00:07:49,333
They did not tell me you had arrived.

76
00:07:52,125 --> 00:07:53,332
What news?

77
00:07:53,333 --> 00:07:55,625
I've had an unexpected visitor.

78
00:07:58,583 --> 00:08:00,666
He has returned already?

79
00:08:04,291 --> 00:08:07,082
Galadriel? Galadriel? Galadriel?

80
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:25,083
Are they not the seeds you planted?

81
00:08:28,291 --> 00:08:30,175
Three rings

82
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:33,125
for the Elven-kings under the sky.

83
00:08:33,916 --> 00:08:38,374
Seven for the Dwarf-lords
in their halls of stone.

84
00:08:38,375 --> 00:08:43,540
Nine for mortal men doomed to die.

85
00:08:56,583 --> 00:08:59,082
We should attack Mordor from the north.

86
00:08:59,083 --> 00:09:02,000
We enter here, between the
Ered Lithui and the Ephel Arnen.

87
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:05,416
It would be wiser to
attack Adar from the east.

88
00:09:06,666 --> 00:09:08,832
What of the whereabouts of Sauron?

89
00:09:08,833 --> 00:09:13,083
Our spies indicate that Sauron was
last seen traveling into Mordor.

90
00:09:13,916 --> 00:09:17,499
We believe he intends to supplant
Adar and claim his armies.

91
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:19,374
If we move swiftly,

92
00:09:19,375 --> 00:09:22,540
we may be able to crush
two spiders with one boot.

93
00:09:22,541 --> 00:09:24,958
And what says the Commander
of the Northern Armies?

94
00:09:25,916 --> 00:09:27,125
Galadriel?

95
00:09:30,375 --> 00:09:33,791
Um, we should send ships up the Anduin,

96
00:09:34,625 --> 00:09:37,500
invade Mordor from the west.

97
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:43,958
See to the preparations.

98
00:09:52,250 --> 00:09:54,374
It does not take the eye of an eagle

99
00:09:54,375 --> 00:09:57,457
to see your thoughts
have flown far afield.

100
00:09:57,458 --> 00:09:59,500
What troubles them?

101
00:10:01,375 --> 00:10:03,625
Sauron may well have traveled to Mordor,

102
00:10:05,625 --> 00:10:07,791
but we cannot be certain
that is where he remains.

103
00:10:09,875 --> 00:10:11,458
What makes you say that?

104
00:10:12,041 --> 00:10:13,166
Sauron...

105
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,791
sees himself not as
master of a barren waste,

106
00:10:18,958 --> 00:10:20,750
but of all Middle-earth.

107
00:10:23,416 --> 00:10:26,000
He seeks to rule it not
only through conquest,

108
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:31,000
but by bending the minds and wills
of all its peoples to his own.

109
00:10:31,583 --> 00:10:33,333
And for that, he needs not armies...

110
00:10:35,333 --> 00:10:36,583
but Rings.

111
00:10:37,333 --> 00:10:40,582
And he cannot craft
them without Celebrimbor.

112
00:10:40,583 --> 00:10:45,666
Sauron is alone, without army or ally.

113
00:10:46,208 --> 00:10:49,915
Eregion is protected by two rivers

114
00:10:49,916 --> 00:10:55,250
with miles of curtain wall of
dwarven stone, ten-foot thick.

115
00:10:56,916 --> 00:11:01,625
Rest assured, Celebrimbor
and the secrets of his craft

116
00:11:02,416 --> 00:11:03,416
are safe.

117
00:11:22,208 --> 00:11:27,708
I tell you, some veiled evil
closes in on Celebrimbor.

118
00:11:28,708 --> 00:11:32,250
Sauron's plan is in motion even now.

119
00:11:32,833 --> 00:11:33,958
I know it.

120
00:11:35,666 --> 00:11:36,875
How?

121
00:11:39,916 --> 00:11:42,500
Since the wearing of
this Ring, I have felt...

122
00:11:44,166 --> 00:11:45,375
perceived...

123
00:11:46,541 --> 00:11:48,750
glimpses of the unseen world...

124
00:11:50,916 --> 00:11:54,541
as dreams unbidden, coming
forth to crowd my waking mind.

125
00:11:56,041 --> 00:11:58,457
You believe the Rings
have kindled your ability

126
00:11:58,458 --> 00:12:01,416
to see that which has
not yet come to pass?

127
00:12:04,291 --> 00:12:05,875
Have they kindled yours?

128
00:12:10,375 --> 00:12:12,541
I have seen mountains crumbling.

129
00:12:13,583 --> 00:12:18,374
Waters running dry. And clouds.
Black. Gathering over white towers.

130
00:12:18,375 --> 00:12:21,290
- Then send me to Eregion.
- Galadriel...

131
00:12:21,291 --> 00:12:24,625
- If Sauron is there, I will send word...
- You cannot face Sauron again.

132
00:12:26,875 --> 00:12:31,124
It is said that once the
Deceiver obtains a being's trust,

133
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:34,500
he gains the ability to
sculpt their very thoughts.

134
00:12:35,083 --> 00:12:39,207
To deceive not only their heart
and mind, but their eyes and ears.

135
00:12:39,208 --> 00:12:41,708
To alter their very reality.

136
00:12:43,041 --> 00:12:45,250
You have already been affected once.

137
00:12:48,250 --> 00:12:49,250
Yes.

138
00:12:50,791 --> 00:12:52,208
He knows my mind.

139
00:12:53,875 --> 00:12:55,333
And I know his.

140
00:12:56,416 --> 00:12:58,541
Which is why I must face him.

141
00:12:59,416 --> 00:13:01,707
Why I alone can slay him.

142
00:13:01,708 --> 00:13:04,207
You once considered him a friend.

143
00:13:04,208 --> 00:13:06,458
- Halbrand was not a...
- Sauron.

144
00:13:07,875 --> 00:13:09,750
You cannot face him alone.

145
00:13:12,125 --> 00:13:14,958
Supposing... I was not alone?

146
00:13:38,750 --> 00:13:43,166
Lord Celebrimbor regrets to inform
you he's unable to grant you entry.

147
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,707
Mightn't I speak with him directly?

148
00:13:46,708 --> 00:13:48,082
My lord is occupied.

149
00:13:48,083 --> 00:13:50,583
But he wishes you good
fortune on your journey.

150
00:13:51,166 --> 00:13:52,833
Are you asking me to leave?

151
00:13:55,125 --> 00:13:57,750
The Lord of Eregion is asking you.

152
00:14:00,166 --> 00:14:02,375
Perhaps I'll just wait here.

153
00:14:06,625 --> 00:14:08,375
Just in case he changes his mind.

154
00:14:23,791 --> 00:14:27,208
- Is he gone?
- No. He refuses to leave, my lord.

155
00:14:30,625 --> 00:14:32,290
Well, he can refuse all he cares to.

156
00:14:32,291 --> 00:14:34,150
I promised Lady
Galadriel before she left

157
00:14:34,151 --> 00:14:36,458
that I would never treat with him again.

158
00:14:40,708 --> 00:14:42,124
Was there something more?

159
00:14:42,125 --> 00:14:44,375
I believe he's injured, my lord.

160
00:14:45,708 --> 00:14:46,916
Let him be.

161
00:14:48,583 --> 00:14:49,583
He'll leave soon enough.

162
00:14:50,541 --> 00:14:53,541
Messengers from Lindon should
arrive with news any day.

163
00:18:23,250 --> 00:18:25,708
What tidings from the white wings?

164
00:18:26,291 --> 00:18:28,291
Sauron's shadow is deepening.

165
00:18:29,041 --> 00:18:33,540
It is said he has taken a new
form to deceive his enemies.

166
00:18:33,541 --> 00:18:34,583
And the Istar?

167
00:18:35,583 --> 00:18:41,375
I hear whispers from salt
scavengers and mûmakil thieves.

168
00:18:42,375 --> 00:18:48,374
Whispers of an old man in rags,
traveling east with two halflings.

169
00:18:48,375 --> 00:18:50,374
He is lost. Vulnerable.

170
00:18:50,375 --> 00:18:52,665
But he will not be for long.

171
00:18:52,666 --> 00:18:55,916
We must reach him before he
learns to harness his powers.

172
00:18:56,833 --> 00:19:00,665
Perhaps, the blood I wasted
to bring you before me

173
00:19:00,666 --> 00:19:05,416
should have been spent
on more useful servants.

174
00:19:11,375 --> 00:19:12,915
Master.

175
00:19:12,916 --> 00:19:15,750
One of the trackers you
sent out has returned.

176
00:19:19,208 --> 00:19:20,540
Have you found him?

177
00:19:20,541 --> 00:19:23,832
I didn't just find him.
I know how to capture him.

178
00:19:23,833 --> 00:19:26,065
Heal the curse upon our flesh,

179
00:19:26,066 --> 00:19:29,541
and I will bring you
the Istar in chains.

180
00:19:30,125 --> 00:19:35,165
What makes you think
a mortal like yourself

181
00:19:35,166 --> 00:19:37,457
could defeat an Istar

182
00:19:37,458 --> 00:19:41,833
when my most powerful
acolytes could not?

183
00:19:42,583 --> 00:19:47,665
The Istar will surrender to
me, because if he doesn't,

184
00:19:47,666 --> 00:19:51,666
I will slaughter the
halflings he calls friends.

185
00:19:55,291 --> 00:19:58,041
What about Doderick?

186
00:20:00,458 --> 00:20:01,749
Doderick?

187
00:20:01,750 --> 00:20:04,874
All right, all right. Andwise?

188
00:20:04,875 --> 00:20:08,791
It is a fine name. Nevertheless,
it is not going to be mine.

189
00:20:10,166 --> 00:20:11,208
I know.

190
00:20:12,125 --> 00:20:13,125
Fredagard.

191
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:16,833
But don't you see?

192
00:20:17,958 --> 00:20:20,166
No one can give you a name.

193
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:22,833
It is yours already.

194
00:20:24,333 --> 00:20:25,875
It is who you are.

195
00:20:27,916 --> 00:20:33,125
And when you hear it spoken,
you feel your heart glow.

196
00:20:34,291 --> 00:20:36,000
You'll hear it one day.

197
00:20:38,333 --> 00:20:39,375
I'm sure of it.

198
00:20:40,875 --> 00:20:42,291
We'll find out who you are.

199
00:20:44,916 --> 00:20:45,999
I knew it!

200
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:47,624
Says here if we turn northeast,

201
00:20:47,625 --> 00:20:50,125
we can cut this leg
of the journey in half.

202
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:52,707
Over there. Come on!

203
00:21:08,791 --> 00:21:10,707
My preference would be to avoid the path

204
00:21:10,708 --> 00:21:12,832
on which we would run
out of water the first day

205
00:21:12,833 --> 00:21:15,125
and die of heat the second.

206
00:21:16,583 --> 00:21:18,666
But perhaps that is just me?

207
00:21:23,041 --> 00:21:24,708
How about Doderick?

208
00:21:26,166 --> 00:21:27,791
You already said Doderick.

209
00:21:30,208 --> 00:21:31,374
No, I didn't.

210
00:21:31,375 --> 00:21:33,166
- Yes, you did.
- Yes, you did.

211
00:21:36,708 --> 00:21:39,375
Ah, how fares the forager this time?

212
00:21:40,291 --> 00:21:43,208
All I found was a scorpion
and a clump of cactus.

213
00:21:43,833 --> 00:21:47,207
The scorpion stung me,
I fell over, and, well...

214
00:21:47,208 --> 00:21:50,000
- That's how I found the cactus.
- That's how you found the cactus.

215
00:21:51,375 --> 00:21:56,000
Couldn't you just, I don't know,
magic some more water into being?

216
00:21:58,500 --> 00:22:02,041
He's afraid he'd lose
control again without a gand.

217
00:22:02,583 --> 00:22:05,000
So we find a gand. S'plenty
of sticks all over the place.

218
00:22:05,541 --> 00:22:07,041
Don't think it works that way, Pop.

219
00:22:07,541 --> 00:22:08,750
Silence.

220
00:22:10,791 --> 00:22:11,875
What is it?

221
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:16,916
On the wind. Can you hear that?

222
00:22:18,541 --> 00:22:20,333
- Almost sounds like...
- Hooves.

223
00:23:32,083 --> 00:23:34,958
They're still close. Mount up!

224
00:23:45,541 --> 00:23:47,000
Who were they?

225
00:23:48,791 --> 00:23:49,916
I don't know.

226
00:23:51,083 --> 00:23:52,541
They're watching our trail.

227
00:23:53,416 --> 00:23:55,583
Meaning, we'd be wise to find another.

228
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,333
We already have.

229
00:24:08,375 --> 00:24:09,583
Nobody goes off-trail.

230
00:24:10,541 --> 00:24:13,041
- Nobody walks alone.
- Nobody walks alone.

231
00:24:33,250 --> 00:24:35,832
Every garden has withered
since the earthquake.

232
00:24:35,833 --> 00:24:37,665
It's not just the gardens.

233
00:24:37,666 --> 00:24:42,041
Rumors abound of dark omens
across all the Dwarven realms.

234
00:24:43,166 --> 00:24:47,124
Some say the mountain was cursed
when the prince let in that Elf.

235
00:24:47,125 --> 00:24:49,874
You two wouldn't be trafficking
in conjecture, would you?

236
00:24:49,875 --> 00:24:51,415
- No.
- Wouldn't dream of it.

237
00:24:51,416 --> 00:24:54,082
Good. 'Cause a rumor's like a songbird.

238
00:24:54,083 --> 00:24:58,250
May sound filling from afar, but
up close, it's an empty feast.

239
00:24:58,958 --> 00:25:00,291
Then it isn't true?

240
00:25:00,958 --> 00:25:03,083
That something terrible is happening?

241
00:25:04,500 --> 00:25:07,041
We're about to prove it isn't.

242
00:25:18,833 --> 00:25:20,457
- King Durin.
- King Durin.

243
00:25:20,458 --> 00:25:21,833
Disa.

244
00:25:23,375 --> 00:25:24,916
Narvi, your report?

245
00:25:25,791 --> 00:25:27,333
Sire.

246
00:25:28,875 --> 00:25:31,958
Not long ago, a fire-mountain awoke.

247
00:25:32,625 --> 00:25:36,832
And although it resides
far to our south,

248
00:25:36,833 --> 00:25:39,624
the ground-shakes it produced

249
00:25:39,625 --> 00:25:44,207
spread through the bones of
the earth all the way here,

250
00:25:44,208 --> 00:25:46,208
collapsing our sun-shafts,

251
00:25:47,125 --> 00:25:50,666
and with them, our
ability to grow crops.

252
00:25:54,208 --> 00:25:56,957
Now, the obvious remedy

253
00:25:56,958 --> 00:25:59,707
is to set the dig-teams to
work repairing the shafts

254
00:25:59,708 --> 00:26:02,249
and sinking new ones. However...

255
00:26:02,250 --> 00:26:04,155
Every Stone-singer you've brought here

256
00:26:04,156 --> 00:26:07,207
has failed to identify
a safe path to dig.

257
00:26:07,208 --> 00:26:09,041
I'm afraid that's true.

258
00:26:11,791 --> 00:26:15,290
With your approval, sire,
we will find the light.

259
00:26:15,291 --> 00:26:16,625
You have it.

260
00:27:23,291 --> 00:27:25,166
For nine centuries,

261
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:32,375
the Stone-singers have fostered
our sacred connection to this rock.

262
00:27:34,041 --> 00:27:38,790
And in all those years, not once,

263
00:27:38,791 --> 00:27:44,875
not once have they ever
ceased to provide for us.

264
00:27:48,541 --> 00:27:52,916
But now, whatever the cause,

265
00:27:55,708 --> 00:27:57,499
the bond is broken.

266
00:27:57,500 --> 00:28:01,582
The hand of darkness has
closed around Khazad-dûm.

267
00:28:01,583 --> 00:28:03,541
Dig carefully, Delve-master.

268
00:28:18,875 --> 00:28:20,208
Disa.

269
00:28:22,125 --> 00:28:23,291
A moment?

270
00:28:32,875 --> 00:28:34,791
Are you really going to make me ask?

271
00:28:36,208 --> 00:28:39,040
Do you mean your
grandchildren? They're well.

272
00:28:39,041 --> 00:28:41,124
They miss tugging your
beard, of course, but...

273
00:28:41,125 --> 00:28:44,416
You needn't make this
harder than it already is.

274
00:28:45,458 --> 00:28:48,125
Funny. I keep saying
the same thing to him.

275
00:28:49,958 --> 00:28:52,999
Surely Durin knows I spoke in anger!

276
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:56,165
If that's an apology I hear,
King, try saying it to my husband.

277
00:28:56,166 --> 00:28:58,458
Why should it be me who apologizes?

278
00:28:59,666 --> 00:29:01,500
It was he who caused offense!

279
00:29:02,958 --> 00:29:04,124
I tell you, he's...

280
00:29:04,125 --> 00:29:07,125
Stubborn as a root-bound parsnip?

281
00:29:08,458 --> 00:29:11,041
One more quality the two
of you have in common.

282
00:29:12,250 --> 00:29:14,541
What you call "stubbornness,"

283
00:29:15,625 --> 00:29:18,291
some Dwarves call "strength."

284
00:29:19,375 --> 00:29:24,875
Oh, I imagine it does take
strength to carry a grudge so heavy.

285
00:29:26,375 --> 00:29:30,833
To keep your wounded heart so
tightly bound, it can barely beat.

286
00:29:33,041 --> 00:29:34,291
Aye, it does.

287
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:39,416
It truly does.

288
00:29:45,166 --> 00:29:47,874
No wonder we can't hear the mountain.

289
00:29:47,875 --> 00:29:50,874
Its King is deaf to the
sorrow of his own son.

290
00:29:50,875 --> 00:29:52,374
Still your axe, Disa!

291
00:29:52,375 --> 00:29:55,291
You want to show true strength?

292
00:29:56,166 --> 00:29:58,041
Summon your son to you.

293
00:30:00,208 --> 00:30:01,541
He'll answer.

294
00:30:03,166 --> 00:30:07,457
But leave it to him and the
peaks of Zirakzigil will thaw

295
00:30:07,458 --> 00:30:09,375
before this feud of yours will.

296
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:17,416
No sunlight yet.

297
00:30:19,250 --> 00:30:20,625
Another dead end.

298
00:30:21,458 --> 00:30:22,957
We're gonna have to work all night.

299
00:30:22,958 --> 00:30:26,040
Oh, here we go.

300
00:30:27,333 --> 00:30:31,583
Growing blisters, I see. No
shame in it. Even I've had 'em.

301
00:30:32,375 --> 00:30:35,415
- Oh, y'have?
- Aye. When I was five!

302
00:30:36,916 --> 00:30:38,540
Aye, palace hands.

303
00:30:38,541 --> 00:30:40,707
Been polishing jewels all his life.

304
00:30:42,416 --> 00:30:45,290
Don't fret, Prince, only 13 hours to go.

305
00:30:45,291 --> 00:30:48,540
Aye. It's his fault we're in this mess.

306
00:30:48,541 --> 00:30:49,750
And his father.

307
00:30:50,833 --> 00:30:51,833
Eh?

308
00:30:54,208 --> 00:30:57,957
Lay a finger on me again, I'll
bite it off at the knuckle.

309
00:31:20,916 --> 00:31:22,083
How was the mine?

310
00:31:26,458 --> 00:31:27,458
'Bout the same.

311
00:31:30,625 --> 00:31:32,040
Where are the weans?

312
00:31:32,041 --> 00:31:34,333
Said they weren't hungry. Again.

313
00:31:34,791 --> 00:31:36,041
Well, I can't blame 'em.

314
00:31:36,833 --> 00:31:39,124
This rye tastes like last year's bread.

315
00:31:39,125 --> 00:31:40,791
It is last year's bread.

316
00:31:42,416 --> 00:31:45,083
Why not trade for fresh
grain from the surface?

317
00:31:45,791 --> 00:31:47,415
Splendid idea!

318
00:31:47,416 --> 00:31:51,124
But who in the Dimrill Dale will we
find to convince your father of it?

319
00:31:51,125 --> 00:31:53,707
- Don't start.
- Um... Let me think...

320
00:31:53,708 --> 00:31:54,915
I said don't.

321
00:31:54,916 --> 00:31:57,582
Ah, climb off your
high peak and apologize!

322
00:31:57,583 --> 00:32:00,540
- You're giving me indigestion.
- Good! Now listen to your guts!

323
00:32:00,541 --> 00:32:01,875
I am!

324
00:32:02,583 --> 00:32:05,124
And they still say I was right.

325
00:32:05,125 --> 00:32:08,540
If he hadn't have
thrown Elrond out to rot,

326
00:32:08,541 --> 00:32:10,707
we'd have food enough for 500 years!

327
00:32:10,708 --> 00:32:12,875
You think this is about food?

328
00:32:15,958 --> 00:32:18,791
We can't hear the mountains anymore.

329
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:26,750
I'm afraid, Durin.

330
00:32:29,541 --> 00:32:30,833
I'm afraid.

331
00:32:31,750 --> 00:32:34,916
Disa... Come here.

332
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:43,416
We're Dwarves.

333
00:32:44,541 --> 00:32:45,958
We'll find a way.

334
00:32:48,458 --> 00:32:50,083
We always have.

335
00:32:51,375 --> 00:32:52,541
How?

336
00:33:17,166 --> 00:33:21,332
Our letters to Celebrimbor
have all gone unanswered.

337
00:33:21,333 --> 00:33:23,458
I fear Sauron may be in Eregion.

338
00:33:24,750 --> 00:33:27,750
The High King has consented to
send me and a small party there,

339
00:33:28,583 --> 00:33:30,791
to ensure Celebrimbor
and his city are safe.

340
00:33:32,916 --> 00:33:34,708
I'm asking you to join us.

341
00:33:37,708 --> 00:33:40,250
As you are so fond of
reminding me, Galadriel,

342
00:33:42,125 --> 00:33:43,415
I am but a politician.

343
00:33:43,416 --> 00:33:45,750
And as such, you have
the High King's trust.

344
00:33:47,375 --> 00:33:48,832
He believes in your steadfastness.

345
00:33:48,833 --> 00:33:52,416
A dog is steadfast. And
quicker to follow on a leash.

346
00:33:59,416 --> 00:34:01,250
He refuses to send me without you.

347
00:34:03,833 --> 00:34:05,000
And why is that?

348
00:34:05,750 --> 00:34:08,166
- You know the reason.
- I'm asking if you know it.

349
00:34:10,166 --> 00:34:15,083
The High King believes, that if
I were to face the Enemy alone,

350
00:34:16,291 --> 00:34:18,041
I may be vulnerable to deception.

351
00:34:18,583 --> 00:34:19,999
And why would he think that?

352
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:21,041
Stop it, Elrond.

353
00:34:23,375 --> 00:34:25,290
You've defied the High
King's orders before.

354
00:34:25,291 --> 00:34:26,875
Why not do so now?

355
00:34:28,458 --> 00:34:29,791
Because he is right.

356
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:32,375
Sauron used me.

357
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:34,975
And under his hand, I
was played like a harp

358
00:34:34,976 --> 00:34:37,041
to a melody not of my choosing.

359
00:34:38,916 --> 00:34:40,916
It was entirely of your choosing.

360
00:34:43,083 --> 00:34:44,874
Sauron looked inside you,

361
00:34:44,875 --> 00:34:48,000
plucked the very song of
your soul, note by note,

362
00:34:49,208 --> 00:34:51,374
making himself out to be
exactly what you needed.

363
00:34:51,375 --> 00:34:53,457
"The Lost King" who
could ride you to victory.

364
00:34:53,458 --> 00:34:56,249
You gave him everything he wanted
and then thanked him for it.

365
00:34:56,250 --> 00:34:58,249
And now he has done
the same to Gil-galad.

366
00:34:58,250 --> 00:34:59,791
And to every Elf in Lindon.

367
00:35:00,958 --> 00:35:04,290
And that is why we need you.
Help us navigate this labyrinth.

368
00:35:04,291 --> 00:35:06,040
There is no navigating it.

369
00:35:06,041 --> 00:35:08,041
The labyrinth is his.

370
00:35:09,416 --> 00:35:11,958
As long as you stay in
it, you've already lost.

371
00:35:13,333 --> 00:35:16,625
- He may well want you in Eregion...
- Please, Elrond.

372
00:35:18,833 --> 00:35:20,791
I cannot let him in again.

373
00:35:22,500 --> 00:35:23,875
I cannot.

374
00:35:46,041 --> 00:35:48,500
He never left, Galadriel.

375
00:35:50,416 --> 00:35:52,750
In choosing to wear those Rings,

376
00:35:53,750 --> 00:35:56,583
you have all chosen to
become his collaborators.

377
00:35:58,291 --> 00:36:00,083
I will have no part in it.

378
00:36:01,708 --> 00:36:03,208
You promised me once,

379
00:36:04,875 --> 00:36:08,458
"If but a whisper of a rumor"
of what I feared proved true,

380
00:36:09,666 --> 00:36:11,833
you would not rest
until it was put right.

381
00:36:14,583 --> 00:36:16,833
If our friendship ever
meant anything to you,

382
00:36:19,708 --> 00:36:20,708
please leave.

383
00:36:49,166 --> 00:36:50,875
Do you not wish to live in beauty?

384
00:36:51,958 --> 00:36:54,790
Master Círdan, I
cannot trust these Rings.

385
00:36:54,791 --> 00:36:57,583
What is beauty, when it
is born, in part, of evil?

386
00:36:58,125 --> 00:36:59,541
No less beautiful.

387
00:37:01,416 --> 00:37:02,582
Not to me.

388
00:37:02,583 --> 00:37:05,415
Would you cast Rúmil's
verses into the flame,

389
00:37:05,416 --> 00:37:07,166
because the poet was a drunkard?

390
00:37:13,250 --> 00:37:14,625
Rúmil was a drunkard?

391
00:37:16,916 --> 00:37:19,541
Do not ask of Daeron.

392
00:37:20,500 --> 00:37:21,791
Insufferable.

393
00:37:23,041 --> 00:37:24,790
But a voice,

394
00:37:24,791 --> 00:37:29,750
a voice that could make the
very sun weep tears of fire.

395
00:37:32,875 --> 00:37:34,375
Judge the work,

396
00:37:36,375 --> 00:37:38,874
and leave judgment concerning
those who wrought it

397
00:37:38,875 --> 00:37:41,832
to the judge who sees all things.

398
00:37:41,833 --> 00:37:43,791
That feels impossible.

399
00:37:45,958 --> 00:37:47,457
It is called humility.

400
00:37:47,458 --> 00:37:49,790
And it is difficult for most.

401
00:37:49,791 --> 00:37:52,250
But it is the truest form of sight.

402
00:38:03,458 --> 00:38:07,125
I wish I could know your peace.

403
00:38:09,541 --> 00:38:10,791
You can.

404
00:38:17,625 --> 00:38:20,957
We do not yet fully
understand these Rings.

405
00:38:20,958 --> 00:38:24,875
But look at the power they
exert over every form of life.

406
00:38:31,250 --> 00:38:35,832
In Sauron's hands, they could
work an evil beyond reckoning,

407
00:38:35,833 --> 00:38:38,750
dominating the minds and wills of all.

408
00:38:39,291 --> 00:38:43,166
This is why they must
remain in the hands of Elves.

409
00:38:45,666 --> 00:38:49,458
You are wise to fear this power, Elrond.

410
00:38:51,875 --> 00:38:56,875
But do not let that fear blind you
to the ways it can be used for good.

411
00:38:59,666 --> 00:39:02,000
For it is not your enemy,
that bears these Rings...

412
00:39:04,125 --> 00:39:08,083
But your most trusted friends.

413
00:39:08,708 --> 00:39:12,707
If you believe they have
strayed, do not abandon them,

414
00:39:12,708 --> 00:39:17,875
but rather open your
eyes and guide them...

415
00:39:18,541 --> 00:39:22,207
Before the darkness
spreads across Middle-earth,

416
00:39:22,208 --> 00:39:24,625
and blinds us all.

417
00:39:57,500 --> 00:39:58,916
You need to rest.

418
00:40:00,541 --> 00:40:03,291
Certainly not, I...

419
00:40:09,958 --> 00:40:11,165
Wake up!

420
00:40:14,833 --> 00:40:17,415
What are you doin'? Get back here!

421
00:40:17,416 --> 00:40:19,499
I saw it. I know I saw it. C'mon.

422
00:40:19,500 --> 00:40:21,291
Poppy, he's not breathin' anymore!

423
00:40:23,666 --> 00:40:25,833
There! Yes! Nori, I can see it!

424
00:40:26,541 --> 00:40:27,957
See what?

425
00:40:27,958 --> 00:40:29,583
Water.

426
00:40:31,458 --> 00:40:35,374
How could someone who
hasn't eaten in so long

427
00:40:35,375 --> 00:40:37,749
still weigh so much?

428
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:42,458
Quick sticks!

429
00:40:45,041 --> 00:40:46,416
Please, oh, please, oh, please.

430
00:40:47,166 --> 00:40:48,291
Hurry, Poppy!

431
00:41:04,625 --> 00:41:05,708
Come on!

432
00:41:15,541 --> 00:41:16,582
I got it.

433
00:41:26,291 --> 00:41:27,540
Come on.

434
00:41:31,166 --> 00:41:32,333
Come on.

435
00:41:33,916 --> 00:41:35,415
You're going to be all right.

436
00:41:39,750 --> 00:41:42,082
Great goats, you're alive.

437
00:41:42,083 --> 00:41:44,916
For a moment there, I thought
we'd lost... we'd lost you.

438
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:53,582
We're none of us, going
to lose each other.

439
00:41:57,875 --> 00:42:00,208
I'd be crying 'cept my eyes are too dry.

440
00:42:08,858 --> 00:42:09,875
Oh...

441
00:42:29,833 --> 00:42:30,875
What is it?

442
00:42:32,625 --> 00:42:33,999
You don't think...

443
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:39,040
It is not dissimilar from
the staff I saw in my dream.

444
00:42:39,041 --> 00:42:41,165
Um, Nori...

445
00:43:05,291 --> 00:43:07,708
Oh, we were just
having a drink of water.

446
00:43:10,583 --> 00:43:11,790
Pängul niganvil!

447
00:43:23,583 --> 00:43:24,915
What are you doin'?

448
00:43:24,916 --> 00:43:25,916
Nori, get down!

449
00:44:18,541 --> 00:44:20,500
Stop! Stop! Make it stop!

450
00:44:26,458 --> 00:44:28,291
Why isn't he stopping it?

451
00:44:28,916 --> 00:44:30,291
He can't!

452
00:44:39,166 --> 00:44:40,416
Help us!

453
00:44:42,083 --> 00:44:43,500
Nori!

454
00:44:45,958 --> 00:44:47,708
I'm coming!

455
00:44:53,041 --> 00:44:57,458
Hold on! Hold on!

456
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:06,208
Nori!

457
00:45:07,166 --> 00:45:08,750
Nori!

458
00:45:20,666 --> 00:45:22,083
It's gone.

459
00:45:24,833 --> 00:45:26,083
Has it?

460
00:45:39,875 --> 00:45:41,749
I have called it ithildin.

461
00:45:41,750 --> 00:45:44,374
Made from our last sliver of mithril.

462
00:45:44,375 --> 00:45:48,208
Out of the moonlight,
it is all but invisible.

463
00:45:49,125 --> 00:45:50,125
It is.

464
00:45:51,916 --> 00:45:53,125
Quite invisible.

465
00:45:59,750 --> 00:46:02,375
Our visitor, is he still...

466
00:46:03,791 --> 00:46:05,958
The night is cold, my lord.

467
00:46:06,833 --> 00:46:09,000
Shall I bring him a shawl?

468
00:47:07,791 --> 00:47:10,875
Whatever the reason
for your presence here,

469
00:47:12,875 --> 00:47:16,250
if you do not leave willingly,
you shall be removed by force.

470
00:47:18,208 --> 00:47:19,833
I can treat with you no longer.

471
00:47:23,333 --> 00:47:24,750
She said you'd say that.

472
00:47:29,375 --> 00:47:32,583
Galadriel? You have spoken with her?

473
00:47:34,083 --> 00:47:35,125
Well, haven't you?

474
00:47:35,666 --> 00:47:36,666
I have not.

475
00:47:37,750 --> 00:47:39,500
Not since she left for Lindon.

476
00:47:40,416 --> 00:47:42,500
Then you know nothing
of what's happened?

477
00:47:43,875 --> 00:47:45,166
Nothing of the Rings?

478
00:47:48,375 --> 00:47:49,750
What of the Rings?

479
00:47:51,833 --> 00:47:52,833
Have they worked?

480
00:47:55,208 --> 00:47:56,750
You'd do better to ask her.

481
00:47:57,250 --> 00:47:58,416
She's not here.

482
00:47:59,541 --> 00:48:02,040
- You are.
- What about the High King?

483
00:48:02,041 --> 00:48:04,916
Surely he wouldn't
neglect to send word of...

484
00:48:06,958 --> 00:48:08,250
Oh, I see.

485
00:48:10,166 --> 00:48:13,375
It's the oldest tale there is, isn't it?

486
00:48:16,375 --> 00:48:19,666
The true creators toil
till their knuckles bleed

487
00:48:20,833 --> 00:48:24,750
and then they come along, take
whatever profits them most,

488
00:48:25,708 --> 00:48:27,458
and forget all about us.

489
00:48:30,666 --> 00:48:32,416
I applaud your patience.

490
00:48:34,541 --> 00:48:36,082
Where are you going?

491
00:48:36,083 --> 00:48:38,500
There's no cause to stay
where I'm not wanted.

492
00:48:40,791 --> 00:48:41,791
Wait.

493
00:48:55,458 --> 00:48:57,583
Halbrand. Please. Tell me.

494
00:48:58,916 --> 00:49:02,833
The Rings. Did they work?

495
00:49:11,708 --> 00:49:13,291
They worked wonders.

496
00:49:17,041 --> 00:49:18,624
Then, the Elves...

497
00:49:18,625 --> 00:49:19,708
Yes.

498
00:49:24,708 --> 00:49:26,915
And, uh, Lindon?

499
00:49:26,916 --> 00:49:28,000
Yes.

500
00:49:35,041 --> 00:49:36,958
- Are you weeping?
- No.

501
00:49:42,583 --> 00:49:44,208
I am reveling.

502
00:49:46,125 --> 00:49:49,083
You have not the slightest inkling...

503
00:49:51,791 --> 00:49:53,290
how this feels.

504
00:49:53,291 --> 00:49:55,707
After all this time,
after so many centuries,

505
00:49:55,708 --> 00:49:58,375
to finally create something.

506
00:50:01,166 --> 00:50:02,875
I'm going to open a First Age bottle.

507
00:50:05,166 --> 00:50:08,291
I have been saving it.

508
00:50:13,875 --> 00:50:15,125
Celebrimbor...

509
00:50:21,625 --> 00:50:22,958
Are you my friend?

510
00:50:24,916 --> 00:50:26,250
Yes, of course.

511
00:50:27,791 --> 00:50:28,832
Why?

512
00:50:28,833 --> 00:50:30,790
Because there is no
place for half-truths

513
00:50:30,791 --> 00:50:33,791
between those who've worked
so close as you and I.

514
00:50:34,791 --> 00:50:35,791
Oh...

515
00:50:37,208 --> 00:50:40,958
And yet there is much you do not know.

516
00:50:42,500 --> 00:50:43,666
Much I want to tell you.

517
00:50:45,458 --> 00:50:46,458
Only...

518
00:50:49,291 --> 00:50:50,750
You're afraid.

519
00:50:52,458 --> 00:50:55,333
You see? I've never been able
to hide anything from you.

520
00:50:56,958 --> 00:50:58,125
Well...

521
00:51:02,750 --> 00:51:04,083
Be at ease.

522
00:51:07,333 --> 00:51:08,501
Whatever it is you wish to say to me,

523
00:51:08,502 --> 00:51:10,583
I shall receive it with an open heart.

524
00:51:13,166 --> 00:51:15,375
I did not come here to
toast the Elven Rings.

525
00:51:17,291 --> 00:51:21,041
But to plead with you
to make Rings for Men.

526
00:51:22,500 --> 00:51:23,833
Rings for Men?

527
00:51:24,791 --> 00:51:26,833
- You saved the Elves.
- Uh...

528
00:51:28,166 --> 00:51:29,291
Elves are not Men.

529
00:51:30,916 --> 00:51:31,916
Men are covetous.

530
00:51:34,208 --> 00:51:36,958
The risks of, of
corruption are far greater.

531
00:51:37,625 --> 00:51:39,290
Even if I did wish to forge more Rings,

532
00:51:39,291 --> 00:51:41,207
the Dwarves would never
provide the mithril.

533
00:51:41,208 --> 00:51:43,915
I think you'll find the Dwarves
facing a dilemma all their own.

534
00:51:43,916 --> 00:51:46,125
What dilemma? What are you
talking about, Halbrand?

535
00:51:48,625 --> 00:51:50,625
My name is not Halbrand.

536
00:51:52,275 --> 00:51:53,291
What?

537
00:51:53,292 --> 00:51:56,000
When Galadriel discovered
the truth, she cast me out.

538
00:51:57,250 --> 00:51:59,415
And I dare not risk the
same happening with you.

539
00:52:03,166 --> 00:52:06,166
I... I take it then you are not a King.

540
00:52:06,958 --> 00:52:09,500
No. Not a King.

541
00:52:10,708 --> 00:52:12,500
Not a Southlander.

542
00:52:13,166 --> 00:52:16,041
Not even a... mortal.

543
00:52:20,000 --> 00:52:21,000
What are you?

544
00:52:22,458 --> 00:52:28,083
There are forces in this
world beyond evil, Celebrimbor.

545
00:52:28,708 --> 00:52:32,375
And sometimes, they send aid,

546
00:52:33,500 --> 00:52:34,790
in the form of an envoy.

547
00:52:34,791 --> 00:52:40,541
A... A messenger, sent to bring
guidance to the ears of the wise.

548
00:52:42,041 --> 00:52:43,041
Uh...

549
00:52:44,500 --> 00:52:46,708
What sort of guidance?

550
00:52:48,083 --> 00:52:50,332
Mordor's rise was but the beginning.

551
00:52:50,333 --> 00:52:52,696
At this very moment,
all Middle-earth balances

552
00:52:52,697 --> 00:52:53,750
on the brink of the abyss.

553
00:52:54,458 --> 00:52:56,791
Soon, every realm will fall.

554
00:52:58,208 --> 00:53:02,500
Not just Elves, but Dwarves. And Men.

555
00:53:04,541 --> 00:53:06,291
The darkness is growing stronger.

556
00:53:07,333 --> 00:53:10,583
And the Rings of Power are our
last hope of restoring the light.

557
00:53:13,791 --> 00:53:15,250
You and I have work to do.

558
00:53:21,542 --> 00:53:24,374
You cannot expect me to believe

559
00:53:24,375 --> 00:53:27,999
that you are a, a messenger
from the Valar sent to...

560
00:53:38,708 --> 00:53:39,916
Halbrand?

561
00:53:42,250 --> 00:53:43,250
Halbrand!

562
00:54:01,750 --> 00:54:02,916
Halbrand!

563
00:54:31,208 --> 00:54:32,401
I have walked through the dust

564
00:54:32,402 --> 00:54:34,583
and the deserts of far-away lands,

565
00:54:37,250 --> 00:54:43,041
in search of an artist possessing
the craft to save all Middle-earth.

566
00:54:45,541 --> 00:54:47,958
A storm is coming, Celebrimbor.

567
00:54:50,250 --> 00:54:53,375
I can bring you the knowledge
none other possesses.

568
00:54:53,958 --> 00:54:57,166
I can unlock your grandest abilities.

569
00:54:57,958 --> 00:55:00,124
And when our work is complete,

570
00:55:00,125 --> 00:55:05,458
never again will the world overlook
you as the mere scion of Fëanor

571
00:55:06,041 --> 00:55:08,333
but forevermore revere you...

572
00:55:14,291 --> 00:55:16,708
The Lord of the Rings.

573
00:55:41,958 --> 00:55:43,666
You need not bow to me.

574
00:55:44,416 --> 00:55:46,500
But I have beheld your natural form.

575
00:55:49,833 --> 00:55:51,000
Rise.

576
00:55:53,708 --> 00:55:55,416
Our work begins now.

577
00:55:56,666 --> 00:55:58,499
What am I to call you?

578
00:55:58,500 --> 00:55:59,666
I am your partner.

579
00:56:02,125 --> 00:56:04,958
No more, no less.

580
00:56:07,000 --> 00:56:08,875
A sharer of gifts.

581
00:56:11,375 --> 00:56:12,916
Annatar.

582
00:56:14,708 --> 00:56:16,166
Annatar.

583
00:56:19,958 --> 00:56:21,666
Lord of Gifts.

584
00:56:38,500 --> 00:56:39,583
You summoned me.

585
00:56:40,416 --> 00:56:42,125
You have new orders, Commander.

586
00:56:42,916 --> 00:56:47,541
You depart for Eregion at first
light, with five of our bravest Elves.

587
00:56:48,708 --> 00:56:49,708
I...

588
00:56:51,708 --> 00:56:54,540
Thank you for reconsidering.

589
00:56:54,541 --> 00:56:56,708
It is not I, you ought to thank.

590
00:56:59,833 --> 00:57:00,916
Elrond.

591
00:57:05,250 --> 00:57:08,458
I am very grateful you have
decided to join my company.

592
00:57:11,208 --> 00:57:13,708
I'm afraid you misunderstand, Galadriel.

593
00:57:14,875 --> 00:57:17,791
Elrond's task is not
to join your company.

594
00:57:18,541 --> 00:57:20,208
But to lead it.

595
00:57:58,458 --> 00:58:00,958
What is it? Is it Elrond?

596
00:58:01,916 --> 00:58:04,708
It's some sort of invitation...

597
00:58:06,250 --> 00:58:08,915
from Lord Celebrimbor.

598
00:58:08,916 --> 00:58:12,041
He wants the Dwarves to come to Eregion.

599
00:58:18,042 --> 00:58:23,042
- Synced and corrected by <font color="#009BCB"><b>chamallow</b></font> -
